Subject: [PATCH] libbe: an app exec()ed by a launched script keeps its port

When the roster launches an application it pre-registers the new team,
creates a looper port for it owned by that team, and sends the launch
messages (B_ARGV_RECEIVED, B_READY_TO_RUN) there. BApplication then drops
its own port and adopts the roster's. That breaks when the file launched
is a script that exec()s the real application -- R Chromium, R Twitter
and the other web-app launchers do exactly that: exec() deletes every
port the team owns, launch messages included, so the BApplication built
after it adopts a port that no longer exists. task_looper() retries the
failing read forever, so the app's main thread uses a whole CPU core in
port_count()/port_buffer_size_etc() returning B_BAD_PORT_ID; nothing sent
to the application arrives, and ReadyToRun() is never called (a stock
DeskCalc started this way shows no window).

Adopt the roster's port only if it is still alive and owned by this team.
Otherwise keep the looper's own port -- the registrar records whatever
port CompleteRegistration() reports -- and post B_ARGV_RECEIVED and
B_READY_TO_RUN to ourselves, as an app that was not pre-registered does.

diff --git a/src/kits/app/Application.cpp b/src/kits/app/Application.cpp
index 8620dbdcc8..6e5ef3d949 100644
--- a/src/kits/app/Application.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/app/Application.cpp
@@ -433,7 +433,17 @@ BApplication::_InitData(const char* signature, bool initGUI, status_t* _error)
 		// we are pre-registered => the app info has been filled in
 		// Check whether we need to replace the looper port with a port
 		// created by the roster.
-		if (appInfo.port >= 0 && appInfo.port != fMsgPort) {
+		// The roster gives that port to the team it launched, and exec()
+		// deletes a team's ports: an app started by a launcher script that
+		// exec()s it would adopt a dead port and spin in task_looper() on
+		// B_BAD_PORT_ID. Keep our own port then; the registrar takes
+		// whatever port CompleteRegistration() reports.
+		port_info portInfo;
+		bool rosterPortGone = appInfo.port >= 0 && appInfo.port != fMsgPort
+			&& (get_port_info(appInfo.port, &portInfo) != B_OK
+				|| portInfo.team != team);
+		if (appInfo.port >= 0 && appInfo.port != fMsgPort
+			&& !rosterPortGone) {
 			delete_port(fMsgPort);
 			fMsgPort = appInfo.port;
 		} else
@@ -444,6 +454,17 @@ BApplication::_InitData(const char* signature, bool initGUI, status_t* _error)
 		// complete the registration
 		fInitError = BRoster::Private().CompleteRegistration(team, thread,
 						appInfo.port);
+		if (fInitError == B_OK && rosterPortGone) {
+			// The launch messages the roster sent (B_ARGV_RECEIVED,
+			// B_READY_TO_RUN) went down with its port; send them ourselves,
+			// as an app that was not pre-registered does.
+			if (__libc_argc > 1) {
+				BMessage argvMessage(B_ARGV_RECEIVED);
+				fill_argv_message(argvMessage);
+				PostMessage(&argvMessage, this);
+			}
+			PostMessage(B_READY_TO_RUN, this);
+		}
 	} else if (fInitError == B_OK) {
 		// not pre-registered -- try to register the application
 		team_id otherTeam = -1;
